    "detailed_description": "This game is a book to browse and read.<br />\r\nIt consists of a collection of images pre-generated by <br />\r\nartificial intelligence, which tell, in a single narrative,<br />\r\nthe four Gospels of the Bible.<br />\r\nThe book begins with the birth of John the Baptist and traces<br />\r\nthe main events of Jesus Christ, narrating his miracles,<br />\r\nquoting the most significant parables, up to the last supper with<br />\r\nhis disciples, his death on the cross and his resurrection.<br />\r\nEach single image automatically scrolls on the screen for a<br />\r\ngeneral overview, then a caption appears to read.<br />\r\nThe aim of the game is to stimulate the reader's imagination for<br />\r\na spiritual reflection on the places and people who<br />\r\nmade the history of that time and knew and lived<br />\r\nwith the Son of God.<br />\r\nWe do not have photographs or films of those historical events but<br />\r\nthanks to artistic representations and new technologies<br />\r\nwe can get an idea of how that reality appeared to men's eyes.<br />\r\nFinally, this is also a way to arouse interest in<br />\r\nreading the Bible and the desire to delve deeper into<br />\r\nthe sacred text of the Gospels.",
